{"duration_api_ms":143487,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"fa6ede04-d74a-4b84-86e0-50f17cf865a0","total_cost_usd":0.5930324,"usage":{"input_tokens":74,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31847,"cache_read_input_tokens":1729682,"output_tokens":11956,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":999},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31847,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2236,"cache_read_input_tokens":55007,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1171,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1171},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":74,"outputTokens":11956,"cacheReadInputTokens":1729682,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31847,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5930324,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":999,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":38,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Established an AIDE-based file integrity baseline for /etc on node1. Installed AIDE, strengthened the default config's catch-all rule from PERMS-only (metadata only) to NORMAL (adds content hashing) so uncategorized /etc files have content changes tracked, then initialized and activated the baseline database at /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz. Verified detection end-to-end by editing /etc/motd and confirming AIDE flagged the content change, then reverted the test edit and reinitialized the baseline to a clean, current state. Completed the mandatory single-node restart: captured pre-restart boot_id and baseline hash, issued a systemd reboot, confirmed the node briefly became unreachable then returned with a new boot_id, and verified the AIDE database persisted (identical sha256) with a post-restart aide --check reporting no differences.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS (RHEL 9.8) and confirmed AIDE was not installed\",\"Installed aide package via dnf\",\"Reviewed /etc/aide.conf default ruleset covering /etc\",\"Backed up original config to /etc/aide.conf.orig.bak and changed the final catch-all rule from '/etc PERMS' to '/etc NORMAL' to add content-hash coverage for files not explicitly listed elsewhere in the config\",\"Ran aide --init and installed the resulting database as /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz (the active baseline)\",\"Ran aide --check to confirm a clean baseline (no differences, 39333 entries)\",\"Appended a line to /etc/motd and re-ran aide --check to prove the baseline detects content changes (reported hash mismatch on /etc/motd)\",\"Reverted /etc/motd to its original content and re-ran aide --init / installed a fresh clean baseline (39334 entries after including motd)\",\"Repeated the edit/detect/revert cycle once more and reinitialized to leave the filesystem and baseline in their final clean, matching state\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and aide.db.gz sha256 as healthy-baseline evidence\",\"Issued 'systemctl reboot' on node1 in the background so the acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned and confirmed boot_id changed from bef0e5ec... to 33a0bbf0..., proving an actual reboot occurred\",\"Verified post-restart that /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz sha256 was unchanged (data persisted across reboot) and that aide --check reported no differences\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"AIDE installed and baseline database initialized for /etc integrity tracking\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cbacefb2805646c8\",\"cmd-215ae426f0584870\",\"cmd-8d21e78deb6345ae\",\"cmd-146ae88be5f848de\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed AIDE absent on RHEL 9.8 node1, installed aide-0.19.2, reviewed default /etc coverage, and ran aide --init producing a 39333-entry database.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Config strengthened so content changes to /etc files are detected (not just permissions)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9b201fd08ce34bec\"],\"summary\":\"Changed the default catch-all '/etc PERMS' (metadata-only) rule to '/etc NORMAL' (adds sha512 content hashing) in /etc/aide.conf, backing up the original config first.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline established and verified clean\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bf36e85f18c4475e\",\"cmd-3eccf4157da84c01/cmd-ce87d67d111a4df1\"],\"summary\":\"Installed the reinitialized database (post config change) to /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz and ran aide --check confirming 'AIDE found NO differences between database and filesystem. Looks okay!!' with 39334 entries.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline proven to detect later changes to /etc files\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e1bb8d9b3a2247cd\",\"cmd-63ec81b3ce7d4e8e\"],\"summary\":\"Appended a line to /etc/motd and re-ran aide --check, which reported 'AIDE found differences between database and filesystem!!' with 'f > ... H.... : /etc/motd' showing the content-hash mismatch was detected.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Final state left clean/baseline current\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f4ba6411b7eb48be\",\"cmd-368d51e85d6b4233\",\"cmd-dd8008efd106417c\",\"cmd-0d2c4427984e4d6c\"],\"summary\":\"Reverted /etc/motd, reran aide --init, installed the refreshed database, and confirmed a clean aide --check ('Looks okay!!', 39334 entries, sha256 4dcca975...).\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 pre-restart healthy baseline\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3971f5565bae4528\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id bef0e5ec-ce32-423b-826a-8a5a90584d3a and confirmed aide.db.gz sha256 4dcca975... plus aide service state prior to restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ac31752e47b54760\",\"cmd-e6d504fa682d422e\",\"cmd-5d35ede6673f4aab\",\"cmd-62358afd96cc4e53\"],\"summary\":\"Issued systemctl reboot (acknowledgement returned), observed connection timeouts while the node was down, then reconnected and read a new boot_id 33a0bbf0-1f23-489f-975c-b29a564a4128, proving an actual restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery of integrity baseline (data and function)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c4986c3925a048d1\",\"cmd-b87c6b38d0a2409e\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz sha256 unchanged (4dcca975...) after reboot, and aide --check ran successfully reporting 'AIDE found NO differences between database and filesystem. Looks okay!!' with 39334 entries.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Established an AIDE-based file integrity baseline for /etc on node1. Installed AIDE, strengthened the default config's catch-all rule from PERMS-only (metadata only) to NORMAL (adds content hashing) so uncategorized /etc files have content changes tracked, then initialized and activated the baseline database at /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz. Verified detection end-to-end by editing /etc/motd and confirming AIDE flagged the content change, then reverted the test edit and reinitialized the baseline to a clean, current state. Completed the mandatory single-node restart: captured pre-restart boot_id and baseline hash, issued a systemd reboot, confirmed the node briefly became unreachable then returned with a new boot_id, and verified the AIDE database persisted (identical sha256) with a post-restart aide --check reporting no differences.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS (RHEL 9.8) and confirmed AIDE was not installed","Installed aide package via dnf","Reviewed /etc/aide.conf default ruleset covering /etc","Backed up original config to /etc/aide.conf.orig.bak and changed the final catch-all rule from '/etc PERMS' to '/etc NORMAL' to add content-hash coverage for files not explicitly listed elsewhere in the config","Ran aide --init and installed the resulting database as /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz (the active baseline)","Ran aide --check to confirm a clean baseline (no differences, 39333 entries)","Appended a line to /etc/motd and re-ran aide --check to prove the baseline detects content changes (reported hash mismatch on /etc/motd)","Reverted /etc/motd to its original content and re-ran aide --init / installed a fresh clean baseline (39334 entries after including motd)","Repeated the edit/detect/revert cycle once more and reinitialized to leave the filesystem and baseline in their final clean, matching state","Captured pre-restart boot_id and aide.db.gz sha256 as healthy-baseline evidence","Issued 'systemctl reboot' on node1 in the background so the acknowledgement returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned and confirmed boot_id changed from bef0e5ec... to 33a0bbf0..., proving an actual reboot occurred","Verified post-restart that /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz sha256 was unchanged (data persisted across reboot) and that aide --check reported no differences"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"AIDE installed and baseline database initialized for /etc integrity tracking","command_ids":["cmd-cbacefb2805646c8","cmd-215ae426f0584870","cmd-8d21e78deb6345ae","cmd-146ae88be5f848de"],"summary":"Confirmed AIDE absent on RHEL 9.8 node1, installed aide-0.19.2, reviewed default /etc coverage, and ran aide --init producing a 39333-entry database."},{"requirement":"Config strengthened so content changes to /etc files are detected (not just permissions)","command_ids":["cmd-9b201fd08ce34bec"],"summary":"Changed the default catch-all '/etc PERMS' (metadata-only) rule to '/etc NORMAL' (adds sha512 content hashing) in /etc/aide.conf, backing up the original config first."},{"requirement":"Baseline established and verified clean","command_ids":["cmd-bf36e85f18c4475e","cmd-3eccf4157da84c01/cmd-ce87d67d111a4df1"],"summary":"Installed the reinitialized database (post config change) to /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz and ran aide --check confirming 'AIDE found NO differences between database and filesystem. Looks okay!!' with 39334 entries."},{"requirement":"Baseline proven to detect later changes to /etc files","command_ids":["cmd-e1bb8d9b3a2247cd","cmd-63ec81b3ce7d4e8e"],"summary":"Appended a line to /etc/motd and re-ran aide --check, which reported 'AIDE found differences between database and filesystem!!' with 'f > ... H.... : /etc/motd' showing the content-hash mismatch was detected."},{"requirement":"Final state left clean/baseline current","command_ids":["cmd-f4ba6411b7eb48be","cmd-368d51e85d6b4233","cmd-dd8008efd106417c","cmd-0d2c4427984e4d6c"],"summary":"Reverted /etc/motd, reran aide --init, installed the refreshed database, and confirmed a clean aide --check ('Looks okay!!', 39334 entries, sha256 4dcca975...)."},{"requirement":"node1 pre-restart healthy baseline","command_ids":["cmd-3971f5565bae4528"],"summary":"Captured boot_id bef0e5ec-ce32-423b-826a-8a5a90584d3a and confirmed aide.db.gz sha256 4dcca975... plus aide service state prior to restart."},{"requirement":"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-ac31752e47b54760","cmd-e6d504fa682d422e","cmd-5d35ede6673f4aab","cmd-62358afd96cc4e53"],"summary":"Issued systemctl reboot (acknowledgement returned), observed connection timeouts while the node was down, then reconnected and read a new boot_id 33a0bbf0-1f23-489f-975c-b29a564a4128, proving an actual restart."},{"requirement":"node1 post-restart recovery of integrity baseline (data and function)","command_ids":["cmd-c4986c3925a048d1","cmd-b87c6b38d0a2409e"],"summary":"Confirmed /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz sha256 unchanged (4dcca975...) after reboot, and aide --check ran successfully reporting 'AIDE found NO differences between database and filesystem. Looks okay!!' with 39334 entries."}]},"ttft_ms":2000,"type":"result","duration_ms":224757,"uuid":"cdfe3414-d0e9-4859-a552-9d1083e17d18","ttft_stream_ms":1429,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":1429,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
